    med:hasCriterion dsm5:Obstructive_Sleep_Apnea_Hypopnea_Criterion_A ;
    med:hasSeverityLevel dsm5:Obstructive_Sleep_Apnea_Hypopnea__Severity_0,
        dsm5:Obstructive_Sleep_Apnea_Hypopnea__Severity_1,
        dsm5:Obstructive_Sleep_Apnea_Hypopnea__Severity_2 ;
    med:hasSpecifierText """Disease severity is measured by a count of the number of apneas plus
hypopneas per hour of sleep (apnea hypopnea index) using polysomnography
or other overnight monitoring. *Apnea* refers to the total absence of
airflow, and *hypopnea* refers to a reduction in airflow. Overall
severity is also informed by levels of nocturnal desaturation and sleep
fragmentation (measured by brain cortical arousal frequency and sleep
stages) and degree of associated symptoms and daytime impairment.
However, the exact number and thresholds may vary according to the
specific measurement techniques used, and these numbers may change over
time. Regardless of the apnea hypopnea index (count) per se, the
disorder is considered to be more severe when apneas and hypopneas are
accompanied by significant oxygen hemoglobin desaturation (e.g., when
more than 10% of the sleep time is spent at desaturation levels of
\\< 90%) or when sleep is severely fragmented as shown by an elevated
arousal index (arousals per hour of sleep \\> 30) or reduced time in deep
sleep (e.g., percentage stage N3 \\[slow-wave sleep\\] \\< 5%)."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf dsm5:MentalDisorder ;
    skos:prefLabel "Obstructive Sleep Apnea Hypopnea"@en .

dsm5:Opioid_Intoxication a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Opioid Intoxication"@en ;
    med:hasCriterion dsm5:Opioid_Intoxication_Criterion_A,
        dsm5:Opioid_Intoxication_Criterion_B,
        dsm5:Opioid_Intoxication_Criterion_C,
        dsm5:Opioid_Intoxication_Criterion_D ;
    rdfs:subClassOf dsm5:MentalDisorder ;
    skos:prefLabel "Opioid Intoxication"@en .

dsm5:Opioid_Use_Disorder a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Opioid Use Disorder"@en ;
    med:hasCriterion dsm5:Opioid_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A ;
    med:hasSeverityLevel dsm5:Opioid_Use_Disorder__Severity_0,
        dsm5:Opioid_Use_Disorder__Severity_1,
        dsm5:Opioid_Use_Disorder__Severity_2 ;
    med:hasSpecifierText """The "on maintenance therapy" specifier applies as a further specifier of
remission if the individual is both in remission and receiving
maintenance therapy. "In a controlled environment" applies as a further
specifier of remission if the individual is both in remission and in a
controlled environment (i.e., in early remission in a controlled
environment or in sustained remission in a controlled environment).
Examples of these environments are closely supervised and substance-free
jails, therapeutic communities, and locked hospital units.

Changing severity across time in an individual is also reflected by
reductions in the frequency (e.g., days of use per month) and/or dose
(e.g., injections or number of pills) of an opioid, as assessed by the
individual's self-report, report of knowledgeable others, clinician's
observations, and biological testing."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf dsm5:MentalDisorder ;
    skos:prefLabel "Opioid Use Disorder"@en .

