dsm5:Childhood_Onset_Fluency_Disorder_Stuttering_Criterion_A a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Childhood-Onset Fluency Disorder (Stuttering) — Criterion A"@en ;
    med:hasMinimumSymptomCount 1 ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Childhood_Onset_Fluency_Disorder_Stuttering_Criterion_A__HP_0000733,
        dsm5:Childhood_Onset_Fluency_Disorder_Stuttering_Criterion_A__HP_0025268,
        dsm5:Childhood_Onset_Fluency_Disorder_Stuttering_Criterion_A__HP_0025774 ;
    rdfs:comment "Disturbances in the normal fluency and time patterning of speech that are inappropriate for the individual's age and language skills, persist over time, and are characterized by frequent and marked occurrences of one (or more) of the following Sound and syllable repetitions. Sound prolongations of consonants as well as vowels. Broken words (e.g., pauses within a word). Audible or silent blocking (filled or unfilled pauses in speech). Circumlocutions (word substitutions to avoid problematic words). Words produced with an excess of physical tension. Monosyllabic whole-word repetitions (e.g., \"I-I-I-I see him\")."@en .

