dsm5:Conduct_Disorder_Criterion_A a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Conduct Disorder — Criterion A"@en ;
    med:hasMinimumSymptomCount 3 ;
    med:hasRequiredDuration "P1Y"^^xsd:duration ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Conduct_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0000718,
        dsm5:Conduct_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0000719,
        dsm5:Conduct_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0008760,
        dsm5:Conduct_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_5200125 ;
    rdfs:comment "A repetitive and persistent pattern of behavior in which the basic rights of others or major age-appropriate societal norms or rules are violated, as manifested by the presence of at least three of the following 15 criteria in the past 12 months from any of the categories below, with at least one criterion present in the past 6 months: <!-- --> **Aggression to People and Animals** Often bullies, threatens, or intimidates others. Often initiates physical fights. Has used a weapon that can cause serious physical harm to others (e.g., a bat, brick, broken bottle, knife, gun). Has been physically cruel to people. Has been physically cruel to animals. Has stolen while confronting a victim (e.g., mugging, purse snatching, extortion, armed robbery). Has forced someone into sexual activity. **Destruction of Property** Has deliberately engaged in fire setting with the intention of causing serious damage. Has deliberately destroyed others' property (other than by fire setting). **Deceitfulness or Theft** Has broken into someone else's house, building, or car. Often lies to obtain goods or favors or to avoid obligations (i.e., \"cons\" others). Has stolen items of nontrivial value without confronting a victim (e.g., shoplifting, but without breaking and entering; forgery). **Serious Violations of Rules** Often stays out at night despite parental prohibitions, beginning before age 13 years. Has run away from home overnight at least twice while living in the parental or parental surrogate home, or once without returning for a lengthy period. Is often truant from school, beginning before age 13 years."@en .

dsm5:Conduct_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0000718 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Aggressive behavior"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0000718 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase describes an aggressive act of forcing someone into sexual activity, which aligns with aggressive behavior."@en .

dsm5:Conduct_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0000719 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Inappropriate behavior"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0000719 ;
    rdfs:comment "Inappropriate behavior encompasses actions such as bullying, threatening, or intimidating others, which aligns with the described behavior."@en .

dsm5:Conduct_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0008760 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
