dsm5:Developmental_Coordination_Disorder_Criterion_C a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Developmental Coordination Disorder — Criterion C"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Onset of symptoms is in the early developmental period"@en .

dsm5:Developmental_Coordination_Disorder_Criterion_D a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Developmental Coordination Disorder — Criterion D"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The motor skills deficits are not better explained by intellectual developmental disorder (intellectual disability) or visual impairment and are not attributable to a neurological condition affecting movement (e.g., cerebral palsy, muscular dystrophy, degenerative disorder)"@en .

dsm5:Disinhibited_Social_Engagement_Disorder_Criterion_A a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Disinhibited Social Engagement Disorder — Criterion A"@en ;
    med:hasMinimumSymptomCount 2 ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Disinhibited_Social_Engagement_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0000745 ;
    rdfs:comment "A pattern of behavior in which a child actively approaches and interacts with unfamiliar adults and exhibits at least two of the following Reduced or absent reticence in approaching and interacting with unfamiliar adults. Overly familiar verbal or physical behavior (that is not consistent with culturally sanctioned and with age-appropriate social boundaries). Diminished or absent checking back with adult caregiver after venturing away, even in unfamiliar settings. Willingness to go off with an unfamiliar adult with minimal or no hesitation."@en .

dsm5:Disinhibited_Social_Engagement_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0000745 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Abnormal diminished volition"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.8 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0000745 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase describes a diminished behavior (checking back with caregiver), which aligns with the concept of diminished volition."@en .

dsm5:Disinhibited_Social_Engagement_Disorder_Criterion_B a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Disinhibited Social Engagement Disorder — Criterion B"@en ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Disinhibited_Social_Engagement_Disorder_Criterion_B__HP_0000734 ;
    rdfs:comment "The behaviors in Criterion A are not limited to impulsivity (as in attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder) but include socially disinhibited behavior"@en .

dsm5:Disinhibited_Social_Engagement_Disorder_Criterion_B__HP_0000734 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Disinhibition"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0000734 ;
    rdfs:comment "Disinhibition is a key aspect of socially disinhibited behavior, which aligns with the DSM-5 criterion."@en .

dsm5:Disinhibited_Social_Engagement_Disorder_Criterion_C a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Disinhibited Social Engagement Disorder — Criterion C"@en ;
    med:hasMinimumSymptomCount 1 ;
    rdfs:comment "The child has experienced a pattern of extremes of insufficient care as evidenced by at least one of the following Social neglect or deprivation in the form of persistent lack of having basic emotional needs for comfort, stimulation, and affection met by caregiving adults. Repeated changes of primary caregivers that limit opportunities to form stable attachments (e.g., frequent changes in foster care). Rearing in unusual settings that severely limit opportunities to form selective attachments (e.g., institutions with high child-to-caregiver ratios)."@en .

dsm5:Disinhibited_Social_Engagement_Disorder_Criterion_D a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Disinhibited Social Engagement Disorder — Criterion D"@en ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Disinhibited_Social_Engagement_Disorder_Criterion_D__HP_5200126 ;
    rdfs:comment "The care in Criterion C is presumed to be responsible for the disturbed behavior in Criterion A (e.g., the disturbances in Criterion A began following the pathogenic care in Criterion C)"@en .

dsm5:Disinhibited_Social_Engagement_Disorder_Criterion_D__HP_5200126 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Aggression towards caregivers"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.8 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_5200126 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase suggests that the disturbed behavior is a result of pathogenic care, which aligns with aggression towards caregivers."@en .

