dsm5:Gambling_Disorder_Criterion_A a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gambling Disorder — Criterion A"@en ;
    med:hasMinimumSymptomCount 4 ;
    med:hasRequiredDuration "P1Y"^^xsd:duration ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Gambling_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0000711,
        dsm5:Gambling_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_5200333,
        dsm5:Gambling_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_5200334 ;
    rdfs:comment "Persistent and recurrent problematic gambling behavior leading to clinically significant impairment or distress, as indicated by the individual exhibiting four (or more) of the following in a 12-month period Needs to gamble with increasing amounts of money in order to achieve the desired excitement. Is restless or irritable when attempting to cut down or stop gambling. Has made repeated unsuccessful efforts to control, cut back, or stop gambling. Is often preoccupied with gambling (e.g., having persistent thoughts of reliving past gambling experiences, handicapping or planning the next venture, thinking of ways to get money with which to gamble). Often gambles when feeling distressed (e.g., helpless, guilty, anxious, depressed). After losing money gambling, often returns another day to get even (\"chasing\" one's losses). Lies to conceal the extent of involvement with gambling. Has jeopardized or lost a significant relationship, job, or educational or career opportunity because of gambling. Relies on others to provide money to relieve desperate financial situations caused by gambling."@en .

dsm5:Gambling_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0000711 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Restlessness"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0000711 ;
    rdfs:comment "Restlessness is a direct match for the feeling of being restless or irritable when attempting to cut down or stop gambling."@en .

dsm5:Gambling_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_5200333 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Addictive spending behavior"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_5200333 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase describes reliance on others for financial support due to gambling issues, which aligns closely with addictive spending behavior."@en .

dsm5:Gambling_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_5200334 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Addictive gambling behavior"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_5200334 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase describes a behavior related to gambling addiction, which aligns with the term for addictive gambling behavior."@en .

dsm5:Gambling_Disorder_Criterion_B a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gambling Disorder — Criterion B"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The gambling behavior is not better explained by a manic episode"@en .

