dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Frontotemporal_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Major or Mild Frontotemporal Neurocognitive Disorder — Criterion C"@en ;
    med:hasMinimumSymptomCount 3 ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Frontotemporal_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C__HP_0000708,
        dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Frontotemporal_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C__HP_0000710,
        dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Frontotemporal_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C__HP_0000733,
        dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Frontotemporal_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C__HP_0000734,
        dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Frontotemporal_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C__HP_0000741,
        dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Frontotemporal_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C__HP_0002463,
        dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Frontotemporal_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C__HP_0033051,
        dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Frontotemporal_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C__HP_5200037 ;
    rdfs:comment "Either (1) or (2) Behavioral variant: Three or more of the following behavioral symptoms: Behavioral disinhibition. Apathy or inertia. Loss of sympathy or empathy. Perseverative, stereotyped or compulsive/ritualistic behavior. Hyperorality and dietary changes. Prominent decline in social cognition and/or executive abilities. Language variant: Prominent decline in language ability, in the form of speech production, word finding, object naming, grammar, or word comprehension."@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Frontotemporal_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C__HP_0000708 a dsm5:Symptom,
