dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Due_to_Traumatic_Brain_Injury_Criterion_A a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Major or Mild Neurocognitive Disorder Due to Traumatic Brain Injury — Criterion A"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The criteria are met for major or mild neurocognitive disorder"@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Due_to_Traumatic_Brain_Injury_Criterion_B a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Major or Mild Neurocognitive Disorder Due to Traumatic Brain Injury — Criterion B"@en ;
    med:hasMinimumSymptomCount 1 ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Due_to_Traumatic_Brain_Injury_Criterion_B__HP_0001289,
        dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Due_to_Traumatic_Brain_Injury_Criterion_B__HP_0007185 ;
    rdfs:comment "There is evidence of a traumatic brain injury---that is, an impact to the head or other mechanisms of rapid movement or displacement of the brain within the skull, with one or more of the following Loss of consciousness. Posttraumatic amnesia. Disorientation and confusion. Neurological signs (e.g., neuroimaging demonstrating injury; visual field cuts; anosmia; hemiparesis; hemisensory loss; cortical blindness; aphasia; apraxia; weakness; loss of balance; other sensory loss that cannot be accounted for by peripheral or other causes)."@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Due_to_Traumatic_Brain_Injury_Criterion_B__HP_0001289 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Confusion"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 1.0 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0001289 ;
    rdfs:comment "Confusion directly matches the clinical phrase 'Disorientation and confusion'."@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Due_to_Traumatic_Brain_Injury_Criterion_B__HP_0007185 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Loss of consciousness"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 1.0 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0007185 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase 'Loss of consciousness' directly matches the HPO term for loss of consciousness."@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Due_to_Traumatic_Brain_Injury_Criterion_C a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Major or Mild Neurocognitive Disorder Due to Traumatic Brain Injury — Criterion C"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The neurocognitive disorder presents immediately after the occurrence of the traumatic brain injury or immediately after recovery of consciousness and persists past the acute post-injury period. Coding note (see coding table on pp. 682--683): For major neurocognitive disorder due to traumatic brain injury, with behavioral disturbance: code first S06.2X9S diffuse traumatic brain injury with loss of consciousness of unspecified duration, sequela; followed by F02.81 major neurocognitive disorder due to traumatic brain injury, with behavioral disturbance. For major neurocognitive disorder due to traumatic brain injury, without behavioral disturbance: code first S06.2X9S diffuse traumatic brain injury with loss of consciousness of unspecified duration, sequela; followed by F02.80 major neurocognitive disorder due to traumatic brain injury, without behavioral disturbance. Note: The severity specifiers \"mild,\" \"moderate,\" and \"severe\" cannot be coded for major neurocognitive disorder but should still be recorded. For mild neurocognitive disorder due to traumatic brain injury, code"@en .

