dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Neurocognitive_Disorder_With_Lewy_Bodies_Criterion_D a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Major or Mild Neurocognitive Disorder With Lewy Bodies — Criterion D"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The disturbance is not better explained by cerebrovascular disease, another neurodegenerative disease, the effects of a substance, or another mental, neurological, or systemic disorder. Coding note (see coding table on pp. 682--683): For major neurocognitive disorder with probable or possible Lewy bodies, with behavioral disturbance, code first G31.83 Lewy body disease, followed by F02.81. For major neurocognitive disorder with probable or possible Lewy bodies, without behavioral disturbance, code first G31.83 Lewy body disease, followed by F02.80. Note: The severity specifiers \"mild,\" \"moderate,\" and \"severe\" cannot be coded for major neurocognitive disorder but should still be recorded. For mild neurocognitive disorder with Lewy bodies, code G31.84"@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_A a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Major or Mild Vascular Neurocognitive Disorder — Criterion A"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The criteria are met for major or mild neurocognitive disorder"@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_B a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Major or Mild Vascular Neurocognitive Disorder — Criterion B"@en ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_B__HP_0001268 ;
    rdfs:comment "The clinical features are consistent with a vascular etiology, as suggested by either of the following Onset of the cognitive deficits is temporally related to one or more cerebrovascular events. Evidence for decline is prominent in complex attention (including processing speed) and frontal-executive function."@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_B__HP_0001268 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Mental deterioration"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0001268 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase describes a decline in cognitive functions, which aligns with the concept of mental deterioration."@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Major or Mild Vascular Neurocognitive Disorder — Criterion C"@en ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C__HP_0006970 ;
    rdfs:comment "There is evidence of the presence of cerebrovascular disease from history, physical examination, and/or neuroimaging considered sufficient to account for the neurocognitive deficits"@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_C__HP_0006970 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Periventricular leukomalacia"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0006970 ;
    rdfs:comment "Periventricular leukomalacia is a type of cerebrovascular disease that can lead to neurocognitive deficits, aligning with the presence of cerebrovascular disease mentioned in the criterion."@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_D a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Major or Mild Vascular Neurocognitive Disorder — Criterion D"@en ;
    med:hasMinimumSymptomCount 1 ;
    rdfs:comment "The symptoms are not better explained by another brain disease or systemic disorder. Probable vascular neurocognitive disorder is diagnosed if one of the following is present; otherwise possible vascular neurocognitive disorder should be diagnosed"@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_E a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Major or Mild Vascular Neurocognitive Disorder — Criterion E"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Clinical criteria are supported by neuroimaging evidence of significant parenchymal injury attributed to cerebrovascular disease (neuroimaging-supported)"@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_F a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Major or Mild Vascular Neurocognitive Disorder — Criterion F"@en ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_F__HP_0001297 ;
    rdfs:comment "The neurocognitive syndrome is temporally related to one or more documented cerebrovascular events"@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_F__HP_0001297 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Stroke"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0001297 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase refers to cerebrovascular events, which directly relates to the HPO term for stroke."@en .

dsm5:Major_or_Mild_Vascular_Neurocognitive_Disorder_Criterion_G a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Major or Mild Vascular Neurocognitive Disorder — Criterion G"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Both clinical and genetic (e.g., cerebral autosomal dominant arteriopathy with subcortical infarcts and leukoencephalopathy) evidence of cerebrovascular disease is present. Possible vascular neurocognitive disorder is diagnosed if the clinical criteria are met but neuroimaging is not available and the temporal relationship of the neurocognitive syndrome with one or more cerebrovascular events is not established. Coding note (see coding table on pp. 682--683): For major neurocognitive disorder probably or possibly due to vascular disease, with behavioral disturbance, code F01.51. For major neurocognitive disorder probably or possibly due to vascular disease, without behavioral disturbance, code F01.50. An additional medical code for the vascular disease is not used. Note: The severity specifiers \"mild,\" \"moderate,\" and \"severe\" cannot be coded for major neurocognitive disorder but should still be recorded"@en .

dsm5:Male_Hypoactive_Sexual_Desire_Disorder_Criterion_A a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Male Hypoactive Sexual Desire Disorder — Criterion A"@en ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Male_Hypoactive_Sexual_Desire_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0025793 ;
    rdfs:comment "Persistently or recurrently deficient (or absent) sexual/erotic thoughts or fantasies and desire for sexual activity. The judgment of deficiency is made by the clinician, taking into account factors that affect sexual functioning, such as age and general and sociocultural contexts of the individual's life"@en .

dsm5:Male_Hypoactive_Sexual_Desire_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0025793 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Abnormal change in sexual drive"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0025793 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase describes a deficiency in sexual thoughts, fantasies, and desire, which aligns with the concept of an abnormal change in sexual drive."@en .

dsm5:Male_Hypoactive_Sexual_Desire_Disorder_Criterion_B a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Male Hypoactive Sexual Desire Disorder — Criterion B"@en ;
    med:hasRequiredDuration "P6M"^^xsd:duration ;
    rdfs:comment "The symptoms in Criterion A have persisted for a minimum duration of approximately 6 months"@en .

dsm5:Male_Hypoactive_Sexual_Desire_Disorder_Criterion_C a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Male Hypoactive Sexual Desire Disorder — Criterion C"@en ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Male_Hypoactive_Sexual_Desire_Disorder_Criterion_C__HP_5200287 ;
