dsm5:Other_or_Unknown_Substance_Intoxication_Criterion_C a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Other (or Unknown) Substance Intoxication — Criterion C"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The signs or symptoms are not attributable to another medical condition and are not better explained by another mental disorder, including intoxication with another substance"@en .

dsm5:Other_or_Unknown_Substance_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Other (or Unknown) Substance Use Disorder — Criterion A"@en ;
    med:hasMinimumSymptomCount 2 ;
    med:hasRequiredDuration "P1Y"^^xsd:duration ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Other_or_Unknown_Substance_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0007086,
        dsm5:Other_or_Unknown_Substance_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0030955,
        dsm5:Other_or_Unknown_Substance_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0033511,
        dsm5:Other_or_Unknown_Substance_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_6000568 ;
    rdfs:comment "A problematic pattern of use of an intoxicating substance not able to be classified within the alcohol; caffeine; cannabis; hallucinogen (phencyclidine and others); inhalant; opioid; sedative, hypnotic, or anxiolytic; stimulant; or tobacco categories and leading to clinically significant impairment or distress, as manifested by at least two of the following, occurring within a 12-month period The substance is often taken in larger amounts or over a longer period than was intended. There is a persistent desire or unsuccessful efforts to cut down or control use of the substance. A great deal of time is spent in activities necessary to obtain the substance, use the substance, or recover from its effects. Craving, or a strong desire or urge to use the substance. Recurrent use of the substance resulting in a failure to fulfill major role obligations at work, school, or home. Continued use of the substance despite having persistent or recurrent social or interpersonal problems caused or exacerbated by the effects of its use. Important social, occupational, or recreational activities are given up or reduced because of use of the substance. Recurrent use of the substance in situations in which it is physically hazardous. Use of the substance is continued despite knowledge of having a persistent or recurrent physical or psychological problem that is likely to have been caused or exacerbated by the substance. Tolerance, as defined by either of the following: A need for markedly increased amounts of the substance to achieve intoxication or desired effect. A markedly diminished effect with continued use of the same amount of the substance. Withdrawal, as manifested by either of the following: The characteristic withdrawal syndrome for other (or unknown) substance (refer to Criteria A and B of the criteria sets for other \\[or unknown\\] substance withdrawal). The substance (or a closely related substance) is taken to relieve or avoid withdrawal symptoms."@en .

dsm5:Other_or_Unknown_Substance_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0007086 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Social and occupational deterioration"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0007086 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase describes a reduction in social and occupational activities due to substance use, which aligns with social and occupational deterioration."@en .

