    rdfs:label "Schizoaffective Disorder — Criterion C"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Symptoms that meet criteria for a major mood episode are present for the majority of the total duration of the active and residual portions of the illness"@en .

dsm5:Schizoaffective_Disorder_Criterion_D a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Schizoaffective Disorder — Criterion D"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The disturbance is not attributable to the effects of a substance (e.g., a drug of abuse, a medication) or another medical condition"@en .

dsm5:Schizoid_Personality_Disorder_Criterion_A a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Schizoid Personality Disorder — Criterion A"@en ;
    med:hasMinimumSymptomCount 4 ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Schizoid_Personality_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0000723,
        dsm5:Schizoid_Personality_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0012154,
        dsm5:Schizoid_Personality_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_4000083,
        dsm5:Schizoid_Personality_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_5200124 ;
    rdfs:comment "A pervasive pattern of detachment from social relationships and a restricted range of expression of emotions in interpersonal settings, beginning by early adulthood and present in a variety of contexts, as indicated by four (or more) of the following Neither desires nor enjoys close relationships, including being part of a family. Almost always chooses solitary activities. Has little, if any, interest in having sexual experiences with another person. Takes pleasure in few, if any, activities. Lacks close friends or confidants other than first-degree relatives. Appears indifferent to the praise or criticism of others. Shows emotional coldness, detachment, or flattened affectivity."@en .

dsm5:Schizoid_Personality_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0000723 a dsm5:Symptom,
