        dsm5:Sedative_Hypnotic_or_Anxiolytic_Intoxication_Criterion_C__HP_0001259,
        dsm5:Sedative_Hypnotic_or_Anxiolytic_Intoxication_Criterion_C__HP_0001350,
        dsm5:Sedative_Hypnotic_or_Anxiolytic_Intoxication_Criterion_C__HP_0002311,
        dsm5:Sedative_Hypnotic_or_Anxiolytic_Intoxication_Criterion_C__HP_0002317,
        dsm5:Sedative_Hypnotic_or_Anxiolytic_Intoxication_Criterion_C__HP_0100543 ;
    rdfs:comment "One (or more) of the following signs or symptoms developing during, or shortly after, sedative, hypnotic, or anxiolytic use Slurred speech. Incoordination. Unsteady gait. Nystagmus. Impairment in cognition (e.g., attention, memory). Stupor or coma."@en .

