dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A a dsm5:DiagnosticCriterion,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Tobacco Use Disorder — Criterion A"@en ;
    med:hasMinimumSymptomCount 2 ;
    med:hasRequiredDuration "P1Y"^^xsd:duration ;
    med:hasSymptom dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0007086,
        dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0030955,
        dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0032500,
        dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0033511,
        dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0033543 ;
    rdfs:comment "A problematic pattern of tobacco use leading to clinically significant impairment or distress, as manifested by at least two of the following, occurring within a 12-month period Tobacco is often taken in larger amounts or over a longer period than was intended. There is a persistent desire or unsuccessful efforts to cut down or control tobacco use. A great deal of time is spent in activities necessary to obtain or use tobacco. Craving, or a strong desire or urge to use tobacco. Recurrent tobacco use resulting in a failure to fulfill major role obligations at work, school, or home (e.g., interference with work). Continued tobacco use despite having persistent or recurrent social or interpersonal problems caused or exacerbated by the effects of tobacco (e.g., arguments with others about tobacco use). Important social, occupational, or recreational activities are given up or reduced because of tobacco use. Recurrent tobacco use in situations in which it is physically hazardous (e.g., smoking in bed). Tobacco use is continued despite knowledge of having a persistent or recurrent physical or psychological problem that is likely to have been caused or exacerbated by tobacco. Tolerance, as defined by either of the following: A need for markedly increased amounts of tobacco to achieve the desired effect. A markedly diminished effect with continued use of the same amount of tobacco. Withdrawal, as manifested by either of the following: The characteristic withdrawal syndrome for tobacco (refer to Criteria A and B of the criteria set for tobacco withdrawal). Tobacco (or a closely related substance, such as nicotine) is taken to relieve or avoid withdrawal symptoms."@en .

dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0007086 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Social and occupational deterioration"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0007086 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase describes a reduction in social and occupational activities due to tobacco use, which aligns with social and occupational deterioration."@en .

dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0030955 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Addictive alcohol use"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.8 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0030955 ;
    rdfs:comment "Withdrawal is often associated with addictive behaviors, making 'Addictive alcohol use' the most relevant term."@en .

dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0032500 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Exacerbated by tobacco use"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0032500 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase indicates that tobacco use continues despite knowledge of problems likely exacerbated by it, which aligns with the term 'Exacerbated by tobacco use'."@en .

dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0033511 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Addictive substance use"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0033511 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase describes a persistent desire or unsuccessful efforts to control tobacco use, which aligns with the concept of addictive substance use."@en .

dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder_Criterion_A__HP_0033543 a dsm5:Symptom,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Addictive nicotine use"@en ;
    dsm5:confidence 0.9 ;
    med:mapsToHPO hpo:HP_0033543 ;
    rdfs:comment "The phrase describes taking tobacco in larger amounts, which aligns with addictive nicotine use."@en .

dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder__Severity_0 a dsm5:SeverityLevel,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "F17.200 Moderate:** Presence of 4--5 symptoms."@en .

dsm5:Tobacco_Use_Disorder__Severity_1 a dsm5:SeverityLevel,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "F17.200 Severe:** Presence of 6 or more symptoms."@en .

