        dsm5:Tobacco_Withdrawal_Criterion_B__HP_0100543,
        dsm5:Tobacco_Withdrawal_Criterion_B__HP_0100785 ;
    rdfs:comment "Abrupt cessation of tobacco use, or reduction in the amount of tobacco used, followed within 24 hours by four (or more) of the following signs or symptoms Irritability, frustration, or anger. Anxiety. Difficulty concentrating. Increased appetite. Restlessness. Depressed mood. Insomnia."@en .

